        <div class="span12">
            <p>
                <a href="#a9t9">a9t9 software</a> was founded in 2016 by two robotic process automation industry veterans.  Earlier, they both founded iOpus Software, which
                is best known for its iMacros browser macro recorder with more than <code>1,000,000 active daily users</code>.
            </p>
            <p>
                a9t9’s company goal is to convert the recent advances in computer vision into usable products for business users and smart hobbyists.
                Our flag-ship products are the popular OCR.space <a href="https://ocr.space">OCR API</a> and <a href="/kantu/web-automation">Kantu</a>, the first visual browser automation tool.
            </p>
            <p>
                The meaning behind the name <em>Kantu</em> is 看圖, which means to look (kàn 看) at pictures/screenshots (tú 圖) in Chinese.
                The idea for Kantu was born out of personal frustration with browser internals. While creating  iMacros was fun and rewarding,  dealing with the many browser internals
                and quirks from IE to Firefox to Chrome became increasingly cumbersome.
                Maybe web developers cannot escape this destiny, but why should users that just want to automate their daily work be dragged into it? <a href="/kantu">Kantu</a> solves this
                problem by using screenshots, OCR and computer vision for robotic process automation.
            </p>
            <p>
                The commercial Editions of our software include free <em>priority</em> tech support. In addition,  we offer custom script 
                and image recognition/computer vision development services for Kantu Enterprise customers. This also includes on-site consulting
                 and training worldwide. Just ask our tech support.
            </p> 
